/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/H3Cys-formation.dat -- a protonation of L-cysteine, written from the master:
      H2Cys + H+  <=>  H3Cys
  Made by bin/curate/species_c373.py from data/curation/batches/species_c373/*.tsv.

  logK25 and dH are the PRINTED values of the sources below (standard state ideal solution at 1 mol/kg, 298.15 K):
      pK1 = 1.71, dH1 = -0.6 kJ/mol (grade CD) [printed as approximate]
      pK2 = 8.36, dH2 = 36.1 kJ/mol, dCp ~-66 J/mol/K (grade BBD)
      pK3 = 10.75, dH3 = 34.1 kJ/mol, dCp ~-204 J/mol/K (grade BBD)
  Source: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231; standard state: hypothetical ideal solution of unit molality, 298.15 K, 0.1 MPa (Section 8, p. 359).
  The master is H2Cys, the form a case declares; this record carries step 1 (the sign flips with the direction written).
  The constant-dCp term of the printed dCp is NOT carried: the record grammar has no place for it (a
  van't Hoff integral with a constant dCp is exactly the `analytic` A1, A3, A4 terms; proposed, not done).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species H3Cys; masters ( { ion H2Cys; nu 1; } { ion H; nu 1; } );
      logK25 1.71; dH 600; source "Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 -- Section 8 summary, p. 359, and Section 7.23, p. 268: pK1 1.71, dH1 -0.6 kJ/mol (pK, dH_ion at 298.15 K)";
